# Plans include docs

Any **plan** created or revised for this project (Plan mode, `.cursor/plans/*.plan.md`, or an implementation checklist) must treat documentation as in-scope work—not a follow-up.

Non-trivial designs also follow `.agents/skills/one-shot-plan/SKILL.md`: one numbered question dump, then a locked plan with no open questions.

## Required in every plan

1. **Docs section or todo** — Name the exact files to create or update (e.g. `docs/FOO.md`, `README.md` “Where do I…?”, folder READMEs under `src/`).
2. **Same PR / same delivery** — Docs land with the feature or design they describe; do not defer to “docs later.”
3. **Truthful status** — If behavior is locked, deferred, or shipped, say so in the doc the plan cites (match patterns in existing `docs/*.md`).

## What to update

| Change type | Typical docs |
| ----------- | ------------ |
| New system / major mechanic | New or existing file under `docs/` + link from README where relevant |
| Contributor workflow / recipe | `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md` and/or the nearest `src/**/README.md` |
| Entry-point discovery | README **“Where do I…?”** table |
| Design-only / pre-implementation | Land the design doc first (see fortifications index pattern) |

## Explicit “no docs” only when

The change is purely internal (typo, test-only, refactor with no player- or contributor-facing behavior) **and** the plan states **Docs: none** with a one-line reason.

## Anti-patterns

- Plan todos for code/tests only, with docs omitted
- “Update docs in a follow-up PR”
- Leaving `docs/` status lines wrong after shipping (e.g. still “deferred” when implemented)
